Fix distributed-write mass termination after transient forward failures
(observed on HCE 2.0 aarch64, packaging repo issue #76):

SendFnPage only attempted a reconnect when the failed forward connection
pointed at a CN (send_to_cn && conn->fail). DN-directed connections never
recover: once conn->fail is set, every subsequent flush proceeds on the
stale socket, SendData fails, and FlushFnBuffer calls
TermFidBackendProc("tcp fails to send data"), which SIGTERMs every
backend holding a local_fid. On a fresh install the first distributed
INSERT then failed with ERROR 57P01 on every attempt until the whole
cluster was restarted; the DN log showed "because tcp fails to send
data, force kill SIGTERM to pid".

Give DN-directed connections the same reconnect treatment the CN path
already has.
--- a/src/backend/forward/fnconn.c
+++ b/src/backend/forward/fnconn.c
@@ -919,6 +919,32 @@
 		}
 
 		conn = &fn_dn_conns[nodeid];
+
+		/*
+		 * Mirror the CN-side handling: when the forward socket to a DN was
+		 * marked failed (receiver restarted, transient network error, ...),
+		 * try to re-establish it before giving up. Without this the stale
+		 * socket makes every subsequent flush fail, and each failure
+		 * terminates all backends holding a local_fid, so one transient TCP
+		 * error kills the whole distributed workload until restart.
+		 */
+		if (conn->fail)
+		{
+			int	fn_send_bulk_bytes = 1024 * FnSendBulkSize;
+
+			if (fnconn_connect_remote(conn, false) == STATUS_OK)
+			{
+				conn->fail = false;
+				add_connection_to_checker(conn);
+				conn->buffer = MemoryContextAlloc(TopMemoryContext, fn_send_bulk_bytes);
+			}
+			else
+			{
+				elog(WARNING, "[SendFnPage] failed to reconnect to forward receiver, name=%s",
+					 NameStr(conn->node.nodename));
+				return false;
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (send_to_cn && conn->fail)
